$DIR/main.p:8:3: cannot pass &local to yield (which may call the loop body at main.p:14), which keeps it after returning
    &local is a pointer to local. local is a local variable of the function
    literal (declared at main.p:7). yield (which may call the loop body at
    main.p:14) stores argument 2 in package variable keep (main.p:15), so &local
    would outlive local.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    If yield (which may call the loop body at main.p:14) should keep its own
    copy of local, change it to take the value, not a pointer, or an owner it
    can keep: an owned[int] from new, a shared[int], or a library owner such as
    a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
